<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles MacCarthy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">killed <a href="/years/1824">1824</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sir Charles MacCarthy, MacCarthy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Charles MacCarthy was a British colonial governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a> settlements in the early nineteenth century. He led a British expedition against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a> and was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nsamankow">Battle of Nsamankow</a> in 1824, when his force was annihilated. His skull was reputedly kept by the Asante as a trophy.</p></div>
